# Release & PR workflow

Pigeon’s in-app **Updates** button compares local `version.py` to **`main`** on GitHub (`pigeon/update_check.py`). Pushing only to `experiment` does **not** ship to devices.

## Branches

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `experiment` | Day-to-day development; push freely |
| `main` | Release line — must match what Updates distributes |

## When the user asks to **push** or **ship** or **release**

1. Ensure `pigeonSystem/pigeon/version.py` `PATCH` was bumped for the code changes.
2. Commit on the working branch (usually `experiment`).
3. `git push -u origin HEAD` for that branch.
4. **If not already on `main`:** open or update a PR into `main`, then merge it (see `RELEASE.md` or run `installer/ship_to_main.sh`).
5. Confirm `main` on GitHub has the new `PATCH` before telling the user Updates will see it.

## Creating the PR (preferred)

From repo root (`/Users/jasonhenley/Desktop/Pigeon`):

```bash
./Pigeon_0.7.0_Development/Pigeon/installer/ship_to_main.sh
```

Or manually:

```bash
gh pr create --base main --head experiment --title "Release 0.7.NN" --body "…"
gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch=false
```

## Do not

- Tell the user Updates will pick up a build that only exists on `experiment`.
- Force-push `main` unless explicitly requested.
- Skip merging to `main` after a release push unless the user only wanted a feature-branch backup.
